e97e0aba9e421a37475a769f9ca1ab2c23b9de25dd25276e4f9fdd70f" :answer-field/choices ["q-135392/selection/bbac105e97e0aba9e421a37475a769f9ca1ab2c23b9de25dd25276e4f9fdd70f" "q-135392/selection/638b8a0094fef0d2bb844b0da55db6628544b9f72543c48b731b7dbfe077c443" "q-135392/selection/bab91e8eb27535c324e6b44b5273f5c01443d45ae992ce317776e5b673d668b5" "q-135392/selection/65271b052f45292ba4a56f7da061be99a0554d5dd1fb9ced38e69bb63dc9718c" "q-135392/selection/3111e0f6d31db244c5c23b0261e8d2349b15a466af10a1492d8d6bc47a7a7298"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-135392" :question/id #uuid "87e7b771-bc37-5691-b9e3-ca79a41f30b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-135392" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the following matrix:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we're given a Frobenius matrix:\n\n- all entries on the main diagonal are ones\n\n- the matrix has only one column (the $1$st column) where some entries below the main diagonal are not zeros\n\n- all the other entries outside the main diagonal are zeros\n\nTo find the inverse of a Frobenius matrix, we simply take the non-zero entries outside the main diagonal with opposite signs. \n\nIn our case, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 1 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-135392/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "77673d0c-9f03-5915-b2ab-4a5d6cb2d94d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-135392"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-135394/selection/905b19025d966ac427d2a934d0c37a33021ddb82dfebfa63f8e337d446b89543" :answer/id #uuid "ee2a9cb9-55c5-5d94-873a-af8f29796329" :answer/type :answer.type/math :a